Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 17:55:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 054/106] ASoC: qcom: q6voice: use the vendor's vocproc
 topologies

The previous commit picked VSS_IVOCPROC_TOPOLOGY_ID_NONE for both
directions, assuming without testing that the stock topologies (echo
cancellation on Tx, the default processing chain on Rx) would fail to
create without calibration data - the pre-existing 'TODO: Implement
calibration' comment they came with suggested as much.

Tested on a POCO X3 NFC: they do not. Vocproc creation and enable ACK
exactly like with the NONE topologies; the only rejected command in
either case is CVP_SET_STEP (RX volume, still needs a calibration
table this port does not load). Topology choice makes no difference to
whether a call comes up silent, so there is no reason to prefer the
passthrough topologies over the vendor's actual choice, which should
give proper echo cancellation and noise suppression once/if the
silence is fixed.
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6cvp.c | 14 ++++++++------
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6cvp.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6cvp.c
index 86dd356e0..fd0b5256e 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6cvp.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6cvp.c
@@ -114,13 +114,15 @@ struct q6voice_session *q6cvp_session_create(enum q6voice_path_type path,
 	cmd.hdr.opcode = VSS_IVOCPROC_CMD_CREATE_FULL_CONTROL_SESSION_V2;
 
 	/*
-	 * The ECNS Tx and default Rx topologies need calibration data from the
-	 * vendor ACDB files, which we do not load. Ask for the NONE topologies,
-	 * a passthrough vocproc that needs no calibration, so voice at least
-	 * flows. (TODO: real calibration for echo cancellation / noise supp.)
+	 * The stock topologies (echo cancellation on Tx, the default
+	 * processing chain on Rx) create and enable the vocproc without any
+	 * error, same as VSS_IVOCPROC_TOPOLOGY_ID_NONE - a passthrough
+	 * topology needs no more calibration than these do for a call to
+	 * come up. Nothing about topology choice makes the difference between
+	 * a silent and a working call, so keep the vendor's actual choice.
 	 */
-	cmd.tx_topology_id = VSS_IVOCPROC_TOPOLOGY_ID_NONE;
-	cmd.rx_topology_id = VSS_IVOCPROC_TOPOLOGY_ID_NONE;
+	cmd.tx_topology_id = VSS_IVOCPROC_TOPOLOGY_ID_TX_SM_ECNS;
+	cmd.rx_topology_id = VSS_IVOCPROC_TOPOLOGY_ID_RX_DEFAULT;
 
 	cmd.direction = VSS_IVOCPROC_DIRECTION_RX_TX;
 	cmd.tx_port_id = tx_port;
